    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9358" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">com-mercor</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">con-m-</span></b> ), ātus, 1, v.
			dep., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to
				trade</i>, <i>traffic together</i>, <i>buy up</i>, <i>purchase</i> (except
			in Sall., only ante - class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">captivos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Capt. prol. 26</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">1, 1, 32</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cives, homines liberos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Pers. 4, 9, 12</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">arma, tela, etc.,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sall. J. 66, 1</span></i>
			.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">commercātus</span></b> , a, um,
			Part. in <i>pass.</i> signif.: edulia,
			Afran. ap. <i><span class="en">Non. p. 28, 30</span></i>.</div>
